! PETSL [MW/m#3/keV]: Longitudinal electron heat loss in SOL: PETSL=q_e/L, 
!  according to G.Becker, NF, Vol.35, No.1, 35 (1995)
!
! (1) Longitudinal heat flux
! q_{e, ||}=-\kappa_{e||}\nabla(T_e)  (Braginski)
! \kappa_{e, ||}=3.16*N_e*T_e*\tau_e/m_e
!
!                  3.11E7 * T_{keV}^(7/2)    3.16           
! q_{e, ||}= ------------------------ * -----  [MW/m^2]
!                 (lambda/10) * L_{||, [m]}   Z_eff
! 
!   (3.16/Z_eff) is replaced with
!  k_0=(4.546+7.732*ZEF)/(0.823+2.44*ZEF+0.62*ZEF**2)
!   3.11E7/(lambda/10)  with  2.13E7
!   \nabla(T_e)   with  T_e/L_||
!  so that
! q_{e, ||}=2.13e7*k_0*T_e^(7/2)/L_||, [keV, m -> MW/m^2]
!
! (2) In addition, heat loss is limited to the free flow value
!
!   q_e=q_{e, ||}*q_FL/(q_{e, ||}+q_FL)
!
! q_FL=C_FL*n_e*m_e*v_e^3, v_e=sqrt(T_e/m_e), C_FL=0.2
!
! q_FL=C_FL*2.12e4*n_13*T_e^(3/2), [keV, 1e13m^-3]
! 
! (3) L=\pi/2*q_a*R_0, L_|| is assumed to be = L
!
!   Usage:  (for implicit scheme)
! PET=...-PETSL
!   (Pereverzev 15-MAR-99)
PETSL = 2.1E4*.2*NE(j)*TE(j)**2.5*(4.546+7.732*ZEF(j))   /(1.E-4*GP*RTOR/MU(NA1)*NE(j)+TE(j)**2)   /(0.823+2.44*ZEF(j)+0.62*ZEF(j)**2)   /(0.5*GP*RTOR/MU(NA1))
